import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Retro — synthesize_rules(rounds=) landed; CONV_FOLD_RULES sweep refuses at truth","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — `synthesize_rules(rounds=)` landed; `CONV_FOLD_RULES` sweep refuses at truth","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/fixpoint-api-and-conv-sweep.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/fixpoint-api-and-conv-sweep.md"}'),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/fixpoint-api-and-conv-sweep.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-synthesize-rules-rounds-landed-conv-fold-rules-sweep-refuses-at-truth" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>synthesize_rules(rounds=)</code> landed; <code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> sweep refuses at truth <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-synthesize-rules-rounds-landed-conv-fold-rules-sweep-refuses-at-truth" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — synthesize_rules(rounds=) landed; CONV_FOLD_RULES sweep refuses at truth”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Follows</strong>: <code>conv-channel-scale-anchor.md</code> (named next step: a fixpoint knob — &quot;depth was the refusal, not material&quot;) and <code>bn-admission-sweep.md</code> (the opt-in families&#39; admission floor). <strong>Commits</strong>: <code>18e82dd</code> (the API + fixpoint tests), <code>62dce40</code> (probe calls the API; the sweep driver), this commit (retro + GOALS).</p><h2 id="item-1-—-the-fixpoint-is-a-real-api-now" tabindex="-1">Item 1 — the fixpoint is a real API now <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-1-—-the-fixpoint-is-a-real-api-now" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 1 — the fixpoint is a real API now”">​</a></h2><p><code>mlopt_core.meta.synthesize_rules</code> gained three knobs; <code>rounds=1</code> is the unchanged single pass (the body moved verbatim to <code>_synthesize_once</code>):</p><ul><li><code>rounds</code> — each round&#39;s emitted stratum feeds back into the bank (<code>usable = base + latest stratum</code>), so a depth-<em>k</em> fold mints within <em>k</em> strata. Loop ends on an empty round, <code>rounds</code> exhausting, or the observer&#39;s veto.</li><li><code>max_emitted</code> — caps the aggregate mint; a round stops minting the moment the cap hits, so the cap bounds <em>validation</em> spend (the dominant cost — derivation replay + fp64 eval), not just list length.</li><li><code>on_round(rnd, stratum)</code> — the per-stratum observer; <code>False</code> stops the fixpoint (caller convergence — the probe&#39;s early-stop-on-fold).</li></ul><p>The returned aggregate dedups cross-round re-mints by alpha key. Measured nuance the docstring pins: a re-mint of an <em>unguarded</em> composite is <code>_subsumed</code> while its stratum is in-bank (synthetic f→g→h→k bank strata alternate 2→1→2); guarded composites cannot subsume, so the probe bank&#39;s strata grow 26→61→242→944 — raw strata 1,273 rows, 974 unique after dedup.</p><p><strong>Probe re-verified end-to-end</strong>: <code>gate_iterated</code> now calls the API and reproduces the mint exactly — fold composite <code>syn_syn_syn_syn_batch_norm_expand__conv_channel_shift_sub_sp_6__conv_ channel_scale_sp_48__conv_channel_scale_l_sp_209__conv_channel_shift_ sp_896</code> in round 4, fires on the real seed, fp64 <code>allclose</code> True (max diff 1.35e-12 vs the fused kernel; the earlier 6.8e-13 figure was the same run&#39;s env draw — both fp64-exact at tol 1e-10).</p><h2 id="item-2-—-the-admission-sweep-truth-starved-not-typed-pay" tabindex="-1">Item 2 — the admission sweep: truth-starved, not typed-pay <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-2-—-the-admission-sweep-truth-starved-not-typed-pay" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 2 — the admission sweep: truth-starved, not typed-pay”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/probes/conv_fold_admission_probe.py</code> stores each rule verbatim (<code>kind=&quot;law&quot;</code>, <code>cert=None</code>) into a scratch store (<code>cache_dir()/conv_fold_admission.db</code>) and runs <code>run_gauntlet</code> over <code>default_gauntlet_corpus()</code> (364 terms / 245 probes / 83 base rules, ~7 s to assemble, 0.2–0.5 s per rule).</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>family</th><th>stage account</th><th>verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> (60)</td><td>reconstruct + full-data pass; measure <code>matches=0</code>; <strong>truth: 0 accepted guarded sites</strong> (synth 0eq/0ne/0rerr over 2000 declined / 2360 envs — the <code>_GUARDED_CAP</code> escalation window included; real 0 accepted, ≤1 declined); <code>derivable=False</code> (no conv premises in <code>ALL_RULES</code>)</td><td><strong>REFUSED at stage 4 (truth)</strong> — all 60, <code>unproven (no evaluable instance)</code>; the 30 <code>nobias</code> variants additionally read <code>numeric=False, view=ill-formed</code> on the raw unguarded verdict (the minted-bias RHS denotes only where the guard accepts)</td></tr><tr><td><code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code> (3)</td><td>unchanged: <code>batch_norm_expand</code> fires=8 typed=8 ill=0 <strong>paid=0</strong>; the two short arities <code>fires=0</code></td><td><strong>REFUSED at stage 6 (typed-pay)</strong> — identical to the recorded sweep; the fixpoint work did not move it</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>The refusal is honest but earlier than expected.</strong> The conv family is fp64-verified <em>true</em> in <code>tests/test_conv_fold_rules.py</code> (incl. <code>groups=2</code>) — the truth gate refused not on a counterexample but on <strong>starvation</strong>: the guarded-region sweep&#39;s synthesized instance bank never produces a coherent <code>conv2d</code> + channel-view site (rank-4 <code>x</code>/<code>W</code> with <code>x[1] == W[1]·groups</code> <em>and</em> <code>sv == (1, W[0], 1, 1)</code> — a corner outside the enumeration&#39;s shape vocabulary, not merely past its default window), and the real corpus has no spelled <code>mul/add/sub(conv2d(…), view)</code> member — aten exports keep the per-channel affine inside <code>batch_norm</code>/<code>conv2d</code>. <code>matches=0</code> so typed-pay never even measured.</p><p>So the family&#39;s value is the one measured last cycle: <strong>discovery enablement</strong> — the anchors are what let the fixpoint mint conv2d-headed composites at all (gate B3&#39;s 944-row stratum is impossible without them). <code>DEFAULT</code> unchanged.</p><h3 id="what-an-enablement-aware-admission-floor-would-require" tabindex="-1">What an &quot;enablement-aware admission floor&quot; would require <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-an-enablement-aware-admission-floor-would-require" aria-label="Permalink to “What an &quot;enablement-aware admission floor&quot; would require”">​</a></h3><ol><li><strong>A truth route that reaches the guarded corner.</strong> Either extend the enumeration bank with the op family&#39;s shape vocabulary (generators that mint coherent <code>conv2d</code>/<code>(1,C,1,1)</code> sites — the channel-view lattice), or drive the sweep from <em>witness bindings</em>: real fold sites the composite fires on (the BN-expanded subgraph positions gate B found), replayed like <code>_seed_witnesses</code> does for validation. Today a guarded corner the bank can&#39;t spell is indistinguishable from an untrue rule — the floor can&#39;t tell &quot;unmeasured&quot; from &quot;false&quot;.</li><li><strong>Premise-of-an-admitted-composite pay accounting.</strong> Admit an anchor when a composite in whose derivation it participates clears the whole gauntlet — fires, typed, <code>paid &gt; 0</code>, closure-safe. The minted fold is the candidate: if the fused-conv member wins extraction on a real conv+BN corpus site, its five-anchor derivation earns admission <em>as a derivation</em> (the anchors ride as premises, not as independently-paying members). Currently unmeasured — that&#39;s the next experiment, not an assumption.</li><li><strong>Guard transport for stored composites</strong> (see below): whatever the floor, a guarded minted composite can&#39;t even reach stage 3 today — its record fails <code>full-data</code>.</li></ol><h3 id="follow-up-measured-composite-guards-vs-law-to-data-rulecache" tabindex="-1">Follow-up measured: composite guards vs <code>law_to_data</code>/<code>rulecache</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#follow-up-measured-composite-guards-vs-law-to-data-rulecache" aria-label="Permalink to “Follow-up measured: composite guards vs law_to_data/rulecache”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>law_to_data</code>: honest refusal — 64/72 minted rules from rounds 1–2 are guarded composites; each reports <code>missing_hooks=(&#39;check&#39;,&#39;derive&#39;)</code>, <code>serializable: False</code>. The <code>_compose_guards</code> closures are procedural by construction, so a guarded minted composite stored as an object <strong>fails <code>full-data</code></strong> — the evidence store cannot carry a transported guard as data today.</li><li><code>rulecache</code>: <strong>partial</strong> — <code>guard_pats</code> + parent names serialize fine, and <code>load(key, base + emitted)</code> round-trips all 72. But the load is all-or-nothing on parent resolution: fixpoint output (round-≥2 parents are <code>syn_*</code> names not in the caller&#39;s bank) <strong>misses entirely against the base ruleset</strong> — one unresolvable parent name returns <code>None</code> for the whole cache, not a partial set. A persisted fixpoint needs either the stratum-aware ruleset passed back (works today) or parent-transitive records (unbuilt).</li></ul><h2 id="test-gate-account" tabindex="-1">Test / gate account <a class="header-anchor" href="#test-gate-account" aria-label="Permalink to “Test / gate account”">​</a></h2><ul><li>New: <code>tests/test_meta_fixpoint.py</code> (6 tests — exact strata, the <code>syn_</code>-parented depth-3 composite firing, cap mid-round and at the boundary, veto, empty stratum, <code>rounds&lt;1</code>).</li><li>Re-ran: <code>test_meta</code>, <code>test_meta_edges</code>, <code>test_synthesis_guards</code>, <code>test_synthesis_seeds</code>, <code>test_rulecache{,_codec}</code>, <code>test_batch_norm_expand</code>, <code>test_conv_fold_rules</code> (114 pass); <code>test_discovery_dspec_synth</code> (68 pass with the above).</li><li><code>ruff check</code>/<code>format</code>, <code>ty</code>, <code>lint-imports</code> clean on touched files; meta.py coverage on the new code is complete under the slice.</li><li>Pre-existing drift (verified at HEAD <code>240a345</code>, not mine): radon baseline vs current radon reports +1–3 cc on seven functions across <code>cond.py</code>/<code>egraph/core.py</code>/<code>meta.py</code>/<code>handler_synth.py</code>; vulture flags <code>tests/test_form_propose.py:142</code>. <code>_synthesize_once</code> was baselined at exactly the moved function&#39;s 51 — a rename, not a ratchet touch.</li></ul><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The fold composite itself is unadmitted — a guarded <code>syn_*</code> object fails <code>full-data</code> today (transported guards aren&#39;t data); running <em>it</em> through the gauntlet is blocked on the serialization item above, not on truth (it fp64-verifies).</li><li><code>synthesize_rules_cached</code> takes no <code>rounds</code>/<code>max_emitted</code> — the cache key would need them in <code>params</code>; not wired (single-round callers unaffected).</li><li><code>on_round</code> returns the stratum by value; a caller that wants to <em>filter</em> feedback (e.g. only guarded composites re-enter) has no hook — measured need first.</li><li>BN&#39;s typed-pay floor and the enablement floor are the same named gap now — one machinery change (premise-of-admitted-composite accounting) would re-measure both families.</li></ul>`,20)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};